   "source": [
    "#Exercise for this Class\n",
    "\n",
    "'''\n",
    "1. Why would we need multiple data types to be stored in same list? Try to think of a real world example\n",
    " and use it in any way you want.()\n",
    " \n",
    "2. Try out a sorting algorithm in Python(any). Below is the code for buble sort in Cpp\n",
    "// C++ Program to how to sort an array\n",
    "\n",
    "#include <algorithm>\n",
    "#include <iostream>\n",
    "using namespace std;\n",
    "\n",
    "int main()\n",
    "{\n",
    "    // Initializing an array\n",
    "    int arr[] = { 5, 4, 1, 2, 3 };\n",
    "\n",
    "    // Calculate the size of the array\n",
    "    int n = sizeof(arr) / sizeof(arr[0]);\n",
    "\n",
    "    // Print the array before sorting the elements\n",
    "    cout << \"Array Before Sorting: \";\n",
    "    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n",
    "        cout << arr[i] << \" \";\n",
    "    }\n",
    "    cout << endl;\n",
    "\n",
    "    // Sort the array\n",
    "    sort(arr, arr + n);\n",
    "\n",
    "    // Print the array after sorting the elements\n",
    "    cout << \"Array After Sorting: \";\n",
    "    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n",
    "        cout << arr[i] << \" \";\n",
    "    }\n",
    "\n",
    "    return 0;\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "3. Task 1\n",
    "\n",
    "a. Write a small python program with some basic calculation functions like add, subtract, \n",
    "divide, min, max etc. All these must be in form of separate functions since these will be used later.\n",
    "You can also print the answer in any format that you want.\n",
    "\n",
    "b. Write another python program to import the file in point1 and use the above functions on user \n",
    "input data to get results. Eg file1.add(1,4) must return 5 in file2.\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "Bonus: Try to explore how a function can take variable number of arguments instead of a \n",
    "fixed number of arguments. Eg. file1.max(1,4) is 4, here we are taking only two arguments i.e 1 and 4.  \n",
    "But we may need to find the max between more than two numbers like max(1,3,4,7) is 7. \n",
    "You may need explore the syntax in python to accommodate this requirement in functions documentation. \n",
    "'''"
   ]
